  "Number": 17,
  "Question": "In the eight term sequence \\(A,\\) \\(B,\\) \\(C,\\) \\(D,\\) \\(E,\\) \\(F,\\) \\(G,\\) \\(H,\\) the value of \\(C\\) is \\(5\\) and the sum of any three consecutive terms is \\(30.\\) What is \\(A+H?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(17\\)",
    "B": "\\(18\\)",
    "C": "\\(25\\)",
    "D": "\\(26\\)",
    "E": "\\(43\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Two neighboring triples share two terms. Since both sums are \\(30\\), canceling those shared terms shows that the term leaving the triple equals the term entering it. Thus terms three places apart are equal.\n\nIn particular,\n\\[\nB+C+D=C+D+E\\implies B=E,\n\\]\nand\n\\[\nE+F+G=F+G+H\\implies E=H.\n\\]\nHence \\(H=B\\). The first triple satisfies \\(A+B+C=30\\), and \\(C=5\\), so\n\\[\nA+H=A+B=30-5=25.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{25}\\), choice C.",
